  "A request from Yosuke-san concerning his sister, Tsukino. A pervert known as the \"Panty Professor\" has been stealing her panties with a drone. I've bought some panties that should lure out the pervert that we'll use to set a trap.": "",
  "A request from Yosuke-san concerning his sister, Tsukino. A pervert known as the \"Panty Professor\" has been stealing her panties with a drone. If I buy some panties, that should lure out the pervert.": "",
  "A request from Yosuke-san concerning his sister, Tsukino. A pervert known as the \"Panty Professor\" had been stealing her panties with a drone. After we lured him out with some panties of our own, we found he was indeed a researcher of sorts, complete with lab coat and everything. No way he was an actual professor... Right? As long as he's gone, that's what matters.": "",
  "Yosuke-san wants me to stop a pervert known as \"Ass Catchem.\" It seems he already groped Tsukino-san, but since the culprit is professional athlete, he ran away with all speed. Tsukino-san has bravely volunteered to lure the pervert out. ": "",
  "Yosuke-san wants me to stop a pervert known as \"Ass Catchem.\" It seems he already groped Tsukino-san, but since the culprit is a professional athlete, he ran away with pure speed. Tsukino-san has bravely volunteered to lure the pervert out. ": "",
  "Yosuke-san asked me to stop a pervert known as \"Ass Catchem.\" It seems he already groped Tsukino-san, but since the culprit is a professional athlete, he ran away with pure speed. Tsukino-san bravely volunteered to lure the pervert out, but as luck would have it, the pervert mistook Yosuke-san for her with short hair and grabbed his ass instead. He'll have some emotional trauma to sort out, but Ass Catchem is off the streets.": "",
  "I got a request from Kawada-san who works at a publishing company called \"Cloudy Skies Publishing.\" He wants me to accompany him to this mystery solving event, solve the puzzle, and win him the publishing rights to Takumi Katagiri's new novel. Just because I'm a detective doesn't mean I can solve puzzles... Curious.": "",
  "I got a request from Kawada-san who works at a publishing company called \"Cloudy Skies Publishing.\" He wanted me to accompany him to this mystery solving event, solve the puzzle, and win him the publishing rights to Takumi Katagiri's new novel. And okay, I solved it, but I still say detectives don't solve puzzles.": "",
  "Another request from Kawada-san from Cloudy Skies Publishing. Turns out the author, Takumi Katagiri, has another puzzle to solve for the rights to a second book. Again with the puzzles...": "",
  "Another request from Kawada-san from Cloudy Skies Publishing. Turns out the author, Takumi Katagiri, had another puzzle to solve for the rights to a second book. I did it again. Maybe detectives <font_kind=yakuza_italic>are</font_kind> meant to solve puzzles...": "",
  "A final request from Kawada-san from Cloudy Skies Publishing. Katagiri's holding another mystery solving event where he'll award the rights to what is apparently the final book in a trilogy? I guess third time's the charm!": "",
  "A final request from Kawada-san from Cloudy Skies Publishing. Katagiri held another mystery solving event where he awarded the rights to what turned out to be the final book in his trilogy. The author has taken quite a shine to Cloudy Skies Publishing, so I think they both have a bright future ahead. As for me, I'm not cut out for the stress of puzzle solving, so I think I'll hang up my top hat.": "",
  "A request from Noriko Taguchi who runs a café in Kamurocho. Her husband had been leaving the house a lot recently and she suspected that he might have been cheating on her. I guess I'll follow the husband and see where it leads.": "",
  "A request from Noriko Taguchi who runs a café in Kamurocho. Her husband has been leaving the house a lot recently and she suspects that he might be cheating on her. I guess I'll follow the husband and see where it leads.": "",
  "A request from Noriko Taguchi who runs a café in Kamurocho. Her husband had been leaving the house a lot recently and she suspected that he might have been cheating on her. Turns out, he was cheating on her with the lady who owned the bar above their café. It's always darkest under the lamppost.": "",
  "A request from Rei Miyamoto-san, who is being sexually harassed at work. Sexual harassment is a delicate subject, and employers don't always make the right calls. That's where I come in. I need to sneak into Miyamoto-san's company and see what proof I can find.": "",
  "A request from Rei Miyamoto-san, who said she was being sexually harassed at work. Sexual harassment is a delicate subject, and employers don't always make the right calls. This case was especially iffy, because the whole thing was a trap set by Miyamoto-san in order to avoid getting transferred out of the office. She really pulled the wool over everyone's eyes, myself included.": "",
  "I was asked by Fumie Taniyama to find her nephew, Hideaki Deguchi. She says she hasn't been able to reach him since he left the house, claiming that he would become the number one host in Kamurocho. He also borrowed half a million yen from her, and it's time he paid her back. I'll find him and collect at the same time.": "",
  "I was asked by Fumie Taniyama to find her nephew, Hideaki Deguchi. She says she hasn't been able to reach him since he left the house, claiming that he would become the number one host in Kamurocho. He also borrowed half a million yen from her, and the stupid kid tried to rob a convenience store in order to pay it back. I was able to stop him, but now he's going to end up working for his uncle on a tuna boat to pay them back. Justice is served, wrapped in seaweed and cucumber.": "",
  "An alien lifeform hovering in the skies... was actually a wig being blown in the wind. The owner of the wig asked me to chase it before the wind blows it who knows where.": "",
  "An alien lifeform hovering in the skies... was actually a wig being blown in the wind. The owner of the wig asked me to chase it, and it turns out his name was Toya Tokunaga, a pop idol. It seems that his personality changes when he doesn't have his wig. Of course the fact that he even wears one is a secret to his fans.": "",
  "I got a strange request from a man named Obayashi, but it was a trap to lure me out, and I got attacked. It seems that the Keihin Gang has put a bounty on me for 10 million yen, and now every thug in town is looking for me. I have to get out of this situation.": "",
  "I got a strange request from a man named Obayashi, but it was a trap to lure me out, and I got attacked. It seems that the Keihin Gang put a bounty on me for 10 million yen, and every thug in town was looking for me. I found the Keihin Gang's hideout and shutdown their whole operation. I was able to get rid of the bounty on my head, but I think the Keihin Gang isn't going anywhere.": "",
  "I became acquainted with Kaito-san's old friend, Adachi-san. Adachi-san seems to run a real estate company in Kamurocho, and he wanted to recruit Kaito-san.": "",
  "I became acquainted with Kaito-san's old friend, Adachi-san. Adachi-san seems to run a real estate company in Kamurocho, and he wanted to recruit Kaito-san. But Adachi was a scumbag who was trying to use him. The rumors about his dirty tactics were true and even though I had to fight Kaito-san about it, we worked together in the end to make Adachi pay.": "",
  "I received a strange request from Hayama-san, who works at a talent agency. He wants me to pretend to be the popular musician, \"Bram-sama\" and divert the media's attention. Apparently \"Bram\" did a lot of bad things when he was a human, and the tabloids want to cover it. Bram-sama himself is very arrogant and a little bit annoying, but it's for the client. I'll endure it.": "",
  "I received a strange request from Hayama-san, who works at a talent agency. He wanted me to pretend to be the popular musician, \"Bram-sama\" and divert the media's attention. Apparently \"Bram\" did a lot of bad things when he was a human, and the tabloids want to cover it. I got our vampire friend in a little trouble, because now Shijima-san has to do community service work, like visiting the old people's home or picking up trash in Kamurocho. I hope he learns a lesson or two about the consequences of being immortal.": "",
  "A search request from Akagawa. He forgot his bag in the public bathroom, and it was gone when he returned for it. There was a jacket in there that was a gift from his brother, and he wants it back, no matter the cost.": "",
  "A search request from Akagawa-san. He forgot his bag in the public bathroom, and it was gone when he returned for it. There was a jacket in there that was a gift from his brother, and he wants it back, no matter the cost.": "",
  "A search request from Akagawa-san. He forgot his bag in the public bathroom, and it was gone when he returned for it. There was a jacket in there that was a gift from his brother, and he wanted it back, no matter the cost. The jacket ended up being thrown away by a hooligan who stole the bag and then picked up by a homeless man. We were able to get it back by giving him warm clothes, but I suggested that Akagawa-san wash it first...": "",
  "Yosuke-san asked me to catch a peeping tom known as \"Judge Creep 'n Peep.\" He apparently takes photos of couples engaging in \"immoral\" sex acts and uploads them on the internet. Yosuke claimed Judge Creep 'n Peep had shots of Tsukino-san with her boyfriend. And I'm told he can crawl along the walls like a cockroach? I can think of a few demon hunting detectives who might be better at this...": "",
  "Yosuke-san asked me to catch a peeping tom known as \"Judge Creep 'n Peep.\" He apparently takes photos of couples engaging in \"immoral\" sex acts and uploads them on the internet. Yosuke claims Judge Creep 'n Peep has shots of Tsukino-san with her boyfriend. And I'm told he can crawl along the walls like a cockroach? I can think of a few demon hunting detectives who might be better at this...": "",
  "Yosuke-san asked me to catch a peeping tom known as \"Judge Creep 'n Peep.\" He apparently takes photos of couples engaging in \"immoral\" sex acts and uploads them on the internet. Yosuke claimed Judge Creep 'n Peep had shots of Tsukino-san with her boyfriend. And yep, he sure crawled like a cockroach, but nothing my drone wasn't able to sort out. More importantly, Yosuke-san lied about Tsukino-san having a boyfriend. Despite having a girlfriend studying abroad, it seems that he was getting it on with a different girl at a hotel. I almost can't blame the \"judge\" for finding him guilty...": "",
  "Megumi Hashimoto-san requested me to investigate if her husband is cheating on her or not. She hired a detective before, but wasn't satisfied with the results, so I'm her second opinion. If the husband is cheating, he may be cautious of detectives, if the previous guy couldn't obtain any evidence. Looks like I'll have to put my own touch on this one.": "",
  "Megumi Hashimoto-san requested me to investigate if her husband is cheating on her or not. She hired a detective before, but wasn't satisfied with the results, so I'm her second opinion. Turns out, the previous detective did get evidence, but he was a crook who sold the info back to the husband. He gives all detectives a bad name.": "",
  "A request from Shoji Ohata. He wants me to find his son who loves to play hide-and-seek. The only clue is the picture sent to Ohata-san from Ayumu-kun. Where did Ayumu-kun hide?": "",
  "A request from Shoji Ohata-san.  He wanted me to find his son who loves to play hide-and-seek. The only clue was the picture sent to Ohata-san from Ayumu-kun. I was able to find the kid, but Ohata-san never came to pick him up. I feel kinda bad for him.": "",
  "Another request from Shoji Ohata. He wants me to find his son who loves to play hide-and-seek again. Once again, the only clue is the picture sent by Ayumu-kun. Where did Ayumu-kun hide this time?": "",
  "Another request from Shoji Ohata-san.  He wants me to find his son who loves to play hide-and-seek again. Once again, the only clue is the picture sent by Ayumu-kun. Where did Ayumu-kun hide this time?": "",
  "Another request from Shoji Ohata-san. He wanted me to find his son who loves to play hide-and-seek. I was able to find him, but what he said has me concerned. Is he hiding in dangerous places on purpose?": "",
  "Another request from Shoji Ohata to find his son. As usual, the only clue is the picture sent to Ohata-san from Ayumu-kun. I better find Ayumu-kun fast. ": "",
  "Another request from Shoji Ohata-san to find his son. As usual, the only clue is the picture sent to Ohata-san from Ayumu-kun. I better find Ayumu-kun fast. ": "",
  "Another request from Shoji Ohata-san to find his son. As usual, the only clue was the picture sent to Ohata-san from Ayumu-kun. In the end, the father came running because he was worried about Ayumu-kun. I'm glad he finally woke up.": "",
  "I was asked to act as a news photographer for a night. The former professional wrestler-turned-politician, \"Gengoro Miki\" is suspected of demanding bribes. Is he gonna sneak a wad of cash into a confection box or something? Or is that just in the movies?": "",
  "I was asked to act as a news photographer for a night. The former professional wrestler-turned-politician, \"Gengoro Miki\" is suspected of demanding bribes. The CEO that Miki was meeting didn't seem to understand that he was supposed to bribe Miki, so he brought him a regular confection box. This pissed Miki off enough to bust out his wrestling moves, which I was all too happy to photograph.": "",
  "A request from Fuyuhiko Tanaka. He told me that one of his subordinates, Asami Morimiya-san, who was being stalked, has disappeared. Could the stalker have done something to her? I have to find Morimiya-san quickly!": "",
  "A request from Fuyuhiko Tanaka. He told me that one of his subordinates, Asami Morimiya-san, who was being stalked, has disappeared, but I've been duped. Turns out the client wasn't the victim's former employer Fuyuhiko Tanaka, but instead was Inamoto, Morimiya's stalker. I really oughta start checking ID.": "",
  "A request from Mamoru Shimazu-san. He wants me to investigate if the property he and his girlfriend are moving into is haunted. Some of the residents claim to have seen a woman with long hair floating around in a white dress. He wants to prove that the property is haunted so he can negotiate lower rent, which I can admire, but... if you take a haunted property, aren't there bigger problems?": "",
  "A request from Mamoru Shimazu-san. He wants me to investigate if the property he and his girlfriend are moving into is haunted. Some of the residents claim to have seen a woman with long hair floating around in a white dress. He wants to prove that the property is haunted so he can negotiate lower rent, which I can admire, but... If you take a haunted property, aren't there bigger problems?": "",
  "A request from Mamoru Shimazu-san. He wanted me to investigate if the property he and his girlfriend are moving into is haunted. Some of the residents claimed to have seen a woman with long hair floating around in a white dress. He was trying to prove that the property was haunted so he could negotiate lower rent, but it turns out that the \"ghost\" was Shimazu's own girlfriend, Yukako-san, who decided to take matters into her own hands. Shimazu-san was overcome with joy to find out his girlfriend went so far to help him, but the landlord was furious. They won't be renting in that building, that's for sure. Not that they seemed to mind. Personally, I just don't want to run into them ever again.": "",
  "A request from Hyuga Kotaro... aka Horny Hinata. He's a comedian who sprung a honeytrap that happened to land him in an article about him having a sexual encounter with an underaged girl, hence the nickname. Maybe it would even work as a comedian? But the sex with a minor allegations are serious, and I guess he wants to avoid jail time. We've got to prove that he's innocent. ": "",
  "A request from Hyuga Kotaro... aka Horny Hinata. He's a comedian who sprung a honeytrap that happened to land him in an article about him having a sexual encounter with an underaged girl, hence the nickname. Maybe it would even work as a comedian? But the sex with a minor allegations are serious, and I guess he wants to avoid jailtime. We've got to prove that he's innocent. ": "",
  "A request from Hyuga Kotaro... aka Horny Hinata. He's a comedian who sprung a honeytrap that happened to land him in an article about him having a sexual encounter with an underaged girl, hence the nickname. Maybe it would even work as a comedian? But the sex with a minor allegations are serious, which is why I managed to prove that it was a trap set up by his own friend, the comedian Kotatsu Higurashi. He even went so far as to get his own girlfriend to sleep with him over it... Money really does rule some hearts, doesn't it?": "",
  "I got an odd request from the owner of Koi Bride. Overnight, some of the carp in the pond had been turned into sashimi. He wants me to find out who did it and why. I can't fathom why anyone would even want koi sashimi...": "",
  "A request from a mysterious man named Shin Amon. He challenged me to a duel for reasons I still don't fully understand. I don't really feel like it, but he's persistent, so I guess I'll indulge him...": "",
  "A request from a mysterious name named Shin Amon. He challenged me to a duel for reasons I still don't fully understand. Amon talked about how he wants to become the strongest man in the city or something. He's a weird guy, but kind of tough all the same.": "",
  "I received a request to look for a cat named \"Zhuang Shi\" by Wang-san. It was a cat owned by the head of his organization who recently passed. The problem is that Zhuang Shi is a \"very valuable\" cat that someone else in the organization is desperately looking for. Is it a tortoiseshell or something? I guess not, but why is this cat so important?": "",
  "I received a request to look for a cat named \"Zhuang Shi\" by Wang-san. It was a cat owned by the head of his organization who recently passed. The problem is that Zhuang Shi isn't just a regular cat, it's a \"very valuable\" cat that someone else in the organization is desperately looking for. Is it a tortoiseshell or something? I guess not, but why is this cat so valuable?": "",
  "I received a request to look for a cat named \"Zhuang Shi\" by Wang-san. It was a cat owned by the head of his organization who recently passed. The problem is that Zhuang Shi isn't just a regular cat, it's a \"very valuable\" cat that someone else in the organization was desperately looking for it. It seems they were after Zhuang Shi's homing instincts, which would lead them back to this dead leader's hideout, and within, his great fortune. But Wang-san didn't even know this, so I think Zhuang Shi and Wang-san will be happy together. If cats are ever truly happy, that is. Who can tell?": "",
  "A request from Shizue Kuwayama-san. She's suspicious that her son's wife might be trying to kill her son. After he married his wife, Kiriko-san, he's had a series of misfortunes, like getting into suspicious accidents or feeling ill. It would almost comical if it weren't true, but I have to trust Shizue-san's instincts here and look into this woman.": "",
  "A request from Shizue Kuwayama-san. She's suspicious that her son's wife might be trying to kill her son. After he married his wife, Kiriko-san, he's had a series of misfortunes, like getting into suspicious accidents or feeling ill. It would almost be comical if it weren't true, but I have to trust Shizue-san's instincts here and look into this woman.": "",
  "A request from Shizue Kuwayama-san. She was suspicious that her son's wife might be trying to kill her son. After he married his wife, Kiriko-san, he's had a series of misfortunes, like getting into suspicious accidents or feeling ill. It would almost be comical if it weren't true, but it was, because Kiriko-san's co-worker, Minami, had unrequited feelings for her. So naturally, he tried to kill her husband. Naturally.": "",
  "Just when we thought the Twisted Trio was down for good, the king of perverts has taken the stage. He's known as \"Giant Impact.\" He flashes his giant genitalia to women, and thus, the name follows. I suppose it's my duty to put him down. Not because I'm jealous or anything...": "",
  "Just when we thought the Twisted Trio was down for good, the king of perverts has taken the stage. He's known as \"Giant Impact.\" He flashes his giant genitalia to women, and thus, the name followed. Strangely enough, Giant Impact turned out to be a 78-year-old virgin, and being celibate that long apparently flipped a switch that was never meant to be flipped. Just because you have something impressive doesn't mean you need to show it off. It's how you use it that matters.": "",
  "There's a bomb in Kamurocho! The bomber is toying with me, and their hint was \"An angel in the warrior's maze.\" I have to stop this!": "",
  "There's a bomb in Kamurocho! The bomber toyed with me, and their hint was \"An angel in the warrior's maze.\" I managed to stop it, but I think they're far from finished...": "",
  "Another bomb! This time the hint is, \"An ox in an inn.\" The bomb is gonna blow in five minutes!": "",
  "Another bomb! This time the hint was, \"An ox in an inn.\" The bomb was set for five minutes, but I got it. But the bomber is still out there...": "",
  "The bomber strikes again! The hint this time is, \"The pigeon coos among the cherry blossoms.\" It's cryptic, but I've only got five minutes!": "",
  "I was able to stop the bomb in time, thanks to Tsukumo. I get where he's coming from about this city's security being so crappy. I mean, I get attacked just because I walk around. But the bombs were too much...": "",
  "I became friends with Sana Mihama-chan who came to Tokyo with a dream to become a singer-songwriter. She sings in Kamurocho in hopes of making her debut. She seems to have a fanbase so maybe it'll work out.": "",
  "I became friends with Sana Mihama-chan who came to Tokyo with a dream to become a singer-songwriter. She sings in Kamurocho in hopes of making her debut, but her producer, Saito, planned on forcing Sana-chan into sleeping with a client, all while filming it to sell as pornography. I was able to save her before she was assaulted, and while she was pretty depressed about the whole thing, her fans encouraged her to keep striving toward her dream.": "",
  "A request from Amane-san. She foresaw that a black calamity would befall a man named Meguro soon... Is this fortune teller the real deal or just a fraud? I'll follow Meguro and see what happens. ": "",
  "A request from Amane-san. She foresaw that a black calamity would befall a man named Meguro soon... And it was a rip-off of a bar called, \"Black Alice.\" I mean, I guess it's black, but my verdict is still out on this fortuneteller.": "",
  "Another request from Amane-san. She foresaw another calamity befall Meguro-san. This time it's a black and white calamity. What kind of calamity could that be? I guess I'll follow Meguro and see what happens...": "",
  "Another request from Amane-san. She foresaw another calamity would befall Meguro-san. This time it's a black and white calamity. What kind of calamity could that be? I guess I'll follow Meguro and see what happens...": "",
  "Another request from Amane-san. She foresaw another calamity would befall Meguro again. This time it was a black and white calamity that turned out to be a police car. Meguro thought Amane-san was causing the misfortunes and attacked her, and I can't help but wonder what would have happened if I hadn't been there to intervene. Or did she predict that too? Sort of chicken and egg, isn't it? I guess this is what you call a self-fulfilling prophecy.": "",
  "Amane-san asked me to protect Hiyama, a man who she foresaw a fire calamity befalling. She said the presence of the calamity has grown massive, and that this was the first time something like this happened. She said she doesn't know how horrible a calamity of this size could be. I'll follow him and hopefully prevent it...": ""
